#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 1320.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134672} :activity/id #uuid "679432e6-e5d0-5d11-9723-5488926e833a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050009 :topic/id #uuid "25fc77a7-3c5b-5da4-a166-1ee95d82e588" :topic/math-academy-id 2123} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134671 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133786 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133595 :question/id #uuid "89a4773c-f6bb-577d-8743-5d0a46c1da6d" :question/math-academy-id "e-5573"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cae73a3-842e-5a1a-8774-35bba342845c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050366}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134250} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134262} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272027} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326795} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326864} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351311} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394181} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481669} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481670} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481672} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488282}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Subspace Spanned by Orthogonal Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "3723cbb7-65e2-58df-a3bc-b3e44a4dbf6d" :step/math-academy-id 20243 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134767}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134672 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135048 :tutorial/content "If $\\big\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 , \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\big\\}$ is a set of orthogonal vectors, then the **orthogonal projection of a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspace $S = \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 , \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\}$** is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+⋯+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{n}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}+\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}+⋯+\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{n}}{{a}_{n}\\cdot {a}_{n}}{a}_{n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto $S = \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 , \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\}$ is the sum of the orthogonal projections of $\\mathbf{x}$ onto each one-dimensional subspace of $\\textrm{Span}\\big\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 , \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\big\\}.$\n\n**Watch out!** The formula works *only* when the set of vectors $\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 , \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\}$ is orthogonal!\n\nIn case of a $2$-dimensional subspace $S=\\textrm{Span} \\big\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2 \\big\\},$ we can visualize the orthogonal projection geometrically, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}\\textrm{proj}_{S} \\: \\mathbf{x}} \n\t= \n\t{\\color{red}\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}_1}\\mathbf{x}} + {\\color{red}\\textrm{proj}_{\\mathbf{a}_2}\\mathbf{x}}\n$$\n\n![](images/7d/7d27747451504c7244ddac4609c9c205c60cd525de2cfd364c20e90c1655ef4e.png)\n\n**Note:** A proof of the formula will be provided at the end of the lesson. But first, let's get some practice using the formula." :tutorial/id #uuid "52ad8222-2949-5d1f-b34c-ea06e2a98ddc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3625 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "bc352e2b-a661-5eae-80e6-33a272fb3132" :step/math-academy-id 20244 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134671}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134673 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133787 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133596 :question/id #uuid "4985be13-9b44-5ec5-b342-00354339b902" :question/math-academy-id "e-5574"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8eb07a32-45bd-5975-9f61-de6294d4895d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048893}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134260} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134269} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272066} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272067} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326861} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326862} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326863} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351463} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351464} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351465} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351466} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373318}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace Spanned by Orthogonal Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "ea84ca60-824b-5c39-820b-45e1a3de351a" :step/math-academy-id 20245 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134773}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134767 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133842 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133657 :question/id #uuid "82a0e170-d916-5ae7-bd72-9b47c7287e0a" :question/math-academy-id "e-7173"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "acb4bd03-9b89-5775-a700-e1f3ea9fa62e" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134305} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134521} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272065} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351336} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351337} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351338} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351339} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373278} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373285} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388674} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392340} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394200}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Orthogonal Projection of a Vector Onto a Plane"} :step/id #uuid "2ffcde54-4ad3-5c96-bc53-f1313d194004" :step/math-academy-id 26414 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134769}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134768 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135087 :tutorial/content "Let's now prove the formula for the orthogonal projection of a vector $\\mathbf{x}$ onto the subspaces $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1 \\}$ and $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_2 \\}$ given that $\\mathbf{a}_1\\perp \\mathbf{a}_2.$ \n\nWe start by writing $\\mathbf{x}$ as a sum of two vectors\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{x}_S + \\mathbf{x}_{S^\\perp},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{x}_S=\\text{proj}_S\\,\\mathbf{x}$ is in $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\},$ and $\\mathbf{x}_{S^\\perp}$ is in the orthogonal complement of $\\textrm{Span}\\{\\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2\\}$. That is, $\\mathbf{x}_S=k_1\\mathbf{a}_1+k_2\\mathbf{a}_2\\in S\\,$ and $\\mathbf{x}_{S^\\perp} \\in S^\\perp.$\n\nFrom the equation above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{{S}^{⊥}} & =x-{x}_{S} \\\\  & =x-({k}_{1}{a}_{1}+{k}_{2}{a}_{2}) \\\\  & =x-{k}_{1}{a}_{1}-{k}_{2}{a}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the fact that $\\mathbf{x}_{S^\\perp}$ is orthogonal to $S,$ and the fact that $\\mathbf{a}_1\\cdot\\mathbf{a}_2=0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{{S}^{⊥}}\\cdot {a}_{1}=0 \\\\ {x}_{{S}^{⊥}}\\cdot {a}_{2}=0\\end{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,⟹\\,\\,\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}(x-{k}_{1}{a}_{1}-{k}_{2}{a}_{2})\\cdot {a}_{1}=0 \\\\ (x-{k}_{1}{a}_{1}-{k}_{2}{a}_{2})\\cdot {a}_{2}=0\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,⟹\\,\\,\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot {a}_{1}-{k}_{1}({a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1})-{k}_{2}({a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{1})=0 \\\\ x\\cdot {a}_{2}-{k}_{1}({a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{2})-{k}_{2}({a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2})=0\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,⟹\\,\\,\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{k}_{1}({a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1})=x\\cdot {a}_{1} \\\\ {k}_{2}({a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2})=x\\cdot {a}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,⟹\\,\\,\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}{k}_{1}=\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}} \\\\ {k}_{2}=\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result, we obtain our formula \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={k}_{1}{a}_{1}+{k}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}+\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2} \\\\  & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "adabdbc0-f726-5b67-81e5-73ef172ea7cf" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4345 :tutorial/title "Justification of the Formula"} :step/id #uuid "5dcbfead-f350-544f-a0c0-5ef1f197ee0f" :step/math-academy-id 26425} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134769 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135088 :tutorial/content "Let $n,m$ be positive integers such that $n\\leq m.$ Given an orthogonal set $\\big\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 , \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\big\\} \\subset  \\Bbb R^m$ and a vector $\\mathbf x \\in \\Bbb R^m,$ we define the **distance between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the vector space $S=\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1,\\mathbf{a}_2,  \\ldots, \\mathbf{a}_n \\}$** as\n\n$$\n\\Vert{ \\color{purple} \\mathbf{x} - \\text{proj}_{S}\\,\\mathbf{x} }\\Vert.\n$$\n\nWe can also define the **angle between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and the subspace $S$** to be the acute angle $\\theta$ between the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ and its orthogonal projection $\\text{proj}_{S}\\,\\mathbf{x},$ as shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/07/07fa0d011bbfd49f89ddc5035a27839640a0c2624046d39fbfe8f57c476b5b25.png)\n\n \n\nFinally, notice that we can represent the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ as a sum of two orthogonal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\underbrace{\\textrm{proj}_{S}\\mathbf{x}}_{\\large \\in S} + \\underbrace{(\\mathbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{S}\\mathbf{x})}_{\\large \\in S^\\perp}\n$$\n\n \n\n**Note:** The vector $\\textbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{S}\\,\\mathbf{x},$ whose norm $\\| \\textbf{x}-\\textrm{proj}_{S}\\,\\mathbf{x} \\|$ represents the distance from $\\mathbf{x}$ to $S,$ is sometimes called the **vector rejection of $\\mathbf{x}$ from $S.$**" :tutorial/id #uuid "0c1861f6-1be0-5e7e-88be-6186634715ef" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4346 :tutorial/title "The Distance Between a Vector and a Subspace"} :step/id #uuid "6328b011-7457-5a1a-b13f-1e2b37822525" :step/math-academy-id 26428 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134673}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134773 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133844 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133659 :question/id #uuid "7014f0ec-9ce3-598a-8ddb-b71a000d383f" :question/math-academy-id "e-7309"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c93bf305-85ff-5455-91ba-ae60f3c1989d" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050336}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134273} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134300} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272093} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326859} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351467} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351468} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351469} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351470} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351473} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351474} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371831} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186481667}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acute Angle Between a Vector and a Subspace Spanned by Orthogonal Vectors"} :step/id #uuid "42dfcb52-37d6-5cd0-9c79-bb0c59437b69" :step/math-academy-id 27054 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134768}}] :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Orthogonal Bases)" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134002}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488338} :activity/id #uuid "6ef06c9d-d12a-5037-973e-b9195cf2afa0" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050009 :topic/id #uuid "25fc77a7-3c5b-5da4-a166-1ee95d82e588" :topic/math-academy-id 2123} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488289 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351338 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1142b8-71d3-5bab-adfc-60cf92d5318c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348567} {:answer/id #uuid "250736d9-adff-5854-90e2-dd99ffdcb9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348765} {:answer/id #uuid "3f2f26ae-b2f0-52d9-b035-6b337eb24c60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349021} {:answer/id #uuid "70221197-9d1a-5f4f-bd40-f730db4ecb4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-11 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349478} {:answer/id #uuid "8c121211-47bd-5e10-9008-c874688472a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -11 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349712}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348567} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9cbfe52-8cc0-5200-b490-45b7c6bbce15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350998}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8bcdeb99-3d44-592c-ac68-43915fe5ae89" :question/math-academy-id "q-81593" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 31\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set $\\{v,w\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-4)+31\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 2+31\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}w=-5\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ -10 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-13 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "07f5fb55-5a96-560a-81bc-2ee4ef08eb3a" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488328}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488315 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326864 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0368bac0-984e-5787-80ab-57f2797279e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324006} {:answer/id #uuid "146ade24-131c-5a2f-b98f-ec8b390c591c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324156} {:answer/id #uuid "8957b4dc-3288-5bc8-94b9-4b3ea2e960ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325143} {:answer/id #uuid "98e891e2-50be-5dde-9dc9-f9157bf702d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325271} {:answer/id #uuid "ab03c3c3-e63d-51f9-b995-161f52c4e24f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325426}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325426} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f98642b-b39d-56b1-9d79-30da4adf0483" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326452}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "3e6b99aa-c1fb-5c62-9a05-f09dd90462a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-40616" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{20\\cdot 4+(-20)\\cdot 5+0\\cdot 0}{{4}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{20}{41}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{20\\cdot 5+(-20)\\cdot (-4)+0\\cdot 0}{{5}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{180}{41}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{20}{41}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{180}{41}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{41}(-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+9\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** The projection is the vector $x$ itself. This means that $x$ can be written as a linear combination of $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In other words, $x$ lies in the subspace spanned by $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$"} :step/id #uuid "81655d18-e7d9-5b1a-ac12-3615ca9b80de" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488319}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488319 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4920a399-1a1b-594a-9001-b155df82b39e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394183} {:answer/id #uuid "24bed580-c0bb-5067-92b0-4c041de3af13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394184} {:answer/id #uuid "5c66e44d-7386-5598-9c1a-fddcb60c5216" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394185} {:answer/id #uuid "45cbe354-7fbf-580c-bfde-cd07d3eee1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394186} {:answer/id #uuid "c8cffea4-3a62-5b3f-abc2-6629aef59007" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394187}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394183} :answer-field/id #uuid "df20fd30-d10b-5edc-90eb-9e19ad4dd340" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394182}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "6ea59652-3e77-5eac-9804-089948d56101" :question/math-academy-id "q-81475" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\},$ $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\},$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\frac{24}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4\\cdot 3+6\\cdot (-5)+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{35}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{4\\cdot 11+6\\cdot 5+3\\cdot 0+(-17)\\cdot (-8)}{{11}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{210}{210}\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -17\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9da9d475-df53-52af-86b4-ac0c78059fca" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488289}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488328 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488282 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d59c73e-d224-5351-a08f-52f78cacb39d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487653} {:answer/id #uuid "3370feb1-25a8-5eb8-998f-be63238ef832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487665} {:answer/id #uuid "47d5bef5-7be7-5c78-9379-5b4b569a0775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487705} {:answer/id #uuid "5e7d0310-d3df-5241-be69-d1e2294cca30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487757} {:answer/id #uuid "f226fba2-029a-5fa4-9d8e-99c484c6060d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488022}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487653} :answer-field/id #uuid "3d54e8d7-80fd-5ba0-9aa1-3d3b5a19b628" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f89a34e2-edc3-5894-bae7-80f53ccb3dc4" :question/math-academy-id "q-140358" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+5\\cdot 1+5\\cdot (-1)}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{1}=-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{3\\cdot (-3)+5\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1}{(-3)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b5a742f9-e91b-50dd-b068-71c2aa9c6666"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488338 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326795 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0212ab39-d874-5d7c-ad86-c2241618470a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323990} {:answer/id #uuid "0f64aa8c-3641-5e89-8274-4f696de0d2e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324114} {:answer/id #uuid "7409f9ea-81b5-5c78-9980-5c9197f99c37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324936} {:answer/id #uuid "783206a7-0741-5713-933e-8355d00c9009" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324970} {:answer/id #uuid "c629928d-112e-5af7-9b8a-91a7d256bc44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325682}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186324936} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ac0593a-15d0-5a5e-9e29-032f810d3b4f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "17b28500-a29b-5fb9-91ad-6adad54b2535" :question/math-academy-id "q-39992" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set \n$\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 2}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{4}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-4)+3\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "de60a247-dd06-59b9-90c3-60ecb2981814" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488315}}] :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Orthogonal Bases)" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487558}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494045} :activity/id #uuid "78343401-39ba-5fb3-a589-44e165c5cb6e" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050009 :topic/id #uuid "25fc77a7-3c5b-5da4-a166-1ee95d82e588" :topic/math-academy-id 2123} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494045 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392340 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3e41f35-f9a3-51af-aed3-cadc7a55cbe9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392342} {:answer/id #uuid "c12aa19b-3eaf-56cc-9bcd-1fd70423d422" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392343} {:answer/id #uuid "e98668e4-b7b4-5165-b775-abfba03a29a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392344} {:answer/id #uuid "8c313108-7af6-5d44-bf88-3edd8fa13470" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{4} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392345} {:answer/id #uuid "79d86d3a-5442-5662-ab8e-bda1a724f157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{2}{5}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392346}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392343} :answer-field/id #uuid "622b7cda-79c9-5c80-96ea-60d2acfa05fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b8a18aba-5bf5-5598-9a5a-e92c825d1e00" :question/math-academy-id "q-40192" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set $\\{v,w\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{3\\cdot (-1)+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}v=\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{3\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=\\frac{11}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{11}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(4\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+11\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a4cae37a-e3ec-588f-b8a6-214967984746" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494064}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494047 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27b82414-74c1-5544-b30e-ddd2ce021c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348789} {:answer/id #uuid "4fd8c6cb-3a96-578f-b2a9-ef7282b4d01c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349168} {:answer/id #uuid "7eadf76b-0b7f-5519-8f83-c78f340e603e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349607} {:answer/id #uuid "d5d514c7-4c99-5779-b25c-30bbeb2dbecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350325} {:answer/id #uuid "e1900fb2-02e4-590c-a21d-1384d20d2199" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350429}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186349607} :answer-field/id #uuid "4df8697c-19ab-5320-a7f6-eea91212521d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350840}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f5a26e7c-2fff-5f64-bdf0-4a1fa47a2fd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81472" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\},$ $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\},$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{0\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-12)\\cdot (-2)}{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 2+(-12)\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{0\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot (-1)+(-12)\\cdot (-2)}{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ac5df48c-0726-5423-8c97-7412ea5b845f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494065}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494064 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134262 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ae601ce-d869-51e6-80bc-284407e6a410" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324067} {:answer/id #uuid "6b523d3f-6e02-5836-b2ce-6c263620bbb3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324865} {:answer/id #uuid "8617a91d-f64d-5379-8961-e1523a360528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325107} {:answer/id #uuid "91b91370-ff8c-5ef3-a9f6-ff6553d43072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325205} {:answer/id #uuid "d9ac762d-1b6e-5391-a5ea-18b12add63fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325867}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325867} :answer-field/id #uuid "0afa59ab-9a94-500b-b0cc-385510a24ddb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326238}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "27fc7f62-58d5-5ef7-b202-bc3a925043e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-40194" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\},$ $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\},$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{7}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{1\\cdot 3+4\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{11}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{1\\cdot 0+4\\cdot (-2)+3\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{11}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(21\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+11\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-8\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ec0f94d1-ae62-5f49-8d28-cff1d955f3ae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494047}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494065 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134521 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c00e40-9e42-5c90-a6ed-b06bba2b0f1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394189} {:answer/id #uuid "d3018d74-c6a7-5472-b968-ca076d6dfada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394190} {:answer/id #uuid "f105f49b-5c70-5ed5-973a-919189de75f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394191} {:answer/id #uuid "0de00c93-be79-5d81-9e17-d6e0e12b193c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394192} {:answer/id #uuid "4ee83998-becb-5e4e-b7f8-f1ca321c259b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394193}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394191} :answer-field/id #uuid "56bdb373-be42-59d0-b26d-244add5ae8da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394188}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "03ed8717-eae6-5c45-8807-fcef562fad7a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81511" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{v,w\\}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set $\\{v,w\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\}$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{10\\cdot (-2)+6\\cdot 1+14\\cdot 3}{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}}v=2\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{10\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (-2)+14\\cdot 2}{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}}w=3\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -6 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ec33a571-16a5-5a2d-8028-b38ef864240e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494069}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186494069 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272027 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9579ba9f-4993-5923-aa2e-30446e774e93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270582} {:answer/id #uuid "ab202d02-1c51-5086-a554-d8b2bc5e1350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270797} {:answer/id #uuid "d2e8fac6-54da-5d4d-a896-efbb467aade2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271125} {:answer/id #uuid "eb77d43d-483f-5926-82a2-e0f053ddcdb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271333}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186270582} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2d867e0-3f81-5ffe-9afd-4d9c3ebaa53e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271804}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "053d8d52-df05-599e-8f48-3e2ea796587b" :question/math-academy-id "q-140120" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ given that the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1}\\},$ $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{2}\\},$ and $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{3}\\}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{7\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 0}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{7\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1+(-1)\\cdot 0+4\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{2}=3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{3}}{{a}_{3}\\cdot {a}_{3}}{a}_{3}=\\frac{7\\cdot (-3)+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 2}{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{2}=-\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{3}}x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "f3b630ff-474b-5c65-b9cb-a6f7547e51ad"}] :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Orthogonal Bases)" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186493377}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518268} :activity/id #uuid "bbfb7477-4df3-54f9-816d-7079bb7ccdb5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050009 :topic/id #uuid "25fc77a7-3c5b-5da4-a166-1ee95d82e588" :topic/math-academy-id 2123} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518226 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373285 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d8597217-e879-5a91-9607-1c6b8944ba4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 11\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373287} {:answer/id #uuid "efef12bf-f408-5a25-a456-76ad7d94c94e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373288} {:answer/id #uuid "51f1110f-3c18-55c8-9ec1-6788d97a8d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -13\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373289} {:answer/id #uuid "45f7982a-75cc-575c-857b-dedc45e412a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373290} {:answer/id #uuid "518c875c-654e-5b51-80ed-b82ea095d7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}." :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373291}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373291} :answer-field/id #uuid "45f3a843-28a3-51eb-bedb-cdde55c51606" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4faefb01-3257-5fa8-9e41-d2b284e76cae" :question/math-academy-id "q-81594" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}15 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{15\\cdot 3+(-3)\\cdot 6+(-3)\\cdot (-12)}{{3}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-12)^{2}}v=\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{15\\cdot 2+(-3)\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}w=4\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "09b16e88-2f98-5aaf-bffe-a62e02c9e116" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518303}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518239 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "595c7e06-3764-50ba-bec9-2bb2d3ec8790" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349268} {:answer/id #uuid "5d8e37ce-0b65-547d-84ec-59a0dfaca58c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349307} {:answer/id #uuid "61659e8c-dc0c-5345-8f4d-2a2cf2f10dc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349339} {:answer/id #uuid "da60a60e-ab26-511f-89ca-0c3669b393ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350363} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ee56a9-520e-5f79-93b1-b6aa6e6c7618" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350578}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186350363} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac760160-44fe-5b46-87a9-67bd6bc761bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "938eaa8d-afe0-5769-ad70-d905f6708ecf" :question/math-academy-id "q-82914" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 1}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-1)+(-3)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 1}{{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}=\\hat{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\hat{x}) & =‖x-\\hat{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\hat{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\hat{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\hat{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\hat{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(2-\\frac{9}{4})}^{2}+{(1-(-\\frac{3}{4}))}^{2}+{(-3-(-\\frac{7}{4}))}^{2}+{(1-\\frac{5}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{49}{16}+\\frac{25}{16}+\\frac{1}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{76}{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "34f06a09-2bb5-52ef-b3bd-ef481b42fe50"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518268 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326862 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23a80ebd-83ac-57fe-8d29-cf9d378a55e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324264} {:answer/id #uuid "8e054025-c750-507e-b378-275bfa2cff6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325176} {:answer/id #uuid "c69c4434-a2aa-5d28-8313-b21b21c08cbd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325687} {:answer/id #uuid "cd6d1a6a-9da2-5d83-aa2c-926093703b2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325754} {:answer/id #uuid "e5f6656e-2e27-5295-8486-ecf5d17ab06b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325996}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186325754} :answer-field/id #uuid "e806f62c-89ec-51c4-a668-7516a58964fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326639}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c22b52e6-cf75-58b2-823a-b76f6234d620" :question/math-academy-id "q-40610" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 4}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{4}^{2}}{a}_{1}=(-\\frac{2}{3})\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2+(-4)\\cdot (-1)}{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{4}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3})\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{4}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}=x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $x$ coincides with the projection, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is zero $0.$"} :step/id #uuid "8cbfaad6-111b-5df3-a75e-eaea87d46a27" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518279}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518279 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351337 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "335b9523-deca-5d75-9645-1d6c085346a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348905} {:answer/id #uuid "3e46f765-0b2a-5a5b-aa2f-fe57b7223392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349016} {:answer/id #uuid "7896d87f-1a14-5e41-95b9-5be658f8e426" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349560} {:answer/id #uuid "d873db20-5652-56e2-8e0e-3fce4bf0bc15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350343} {:answer/id #uuid "dd092b3c-8771-57e2-8990-445d555aa3f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350378}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348905} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9fe258c-56e4-5ca0-ba85-c092749a9d1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "cf535ed1-7a3f-5586-9dd6-0d4749a3c85c" :question/math-academy-id "q-81591" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the plane $r=sv+tw,$ where $s,t\\in R,$ and\n\n$$\nv=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,w=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the plane given that $v⊥w.$" :question/worked-solution "Since our plane passes through the origin, it defines the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{v,w}$ in ${R}^{3}.$ \nAnd, since the set ${v,w}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by \n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot v}{v\\cdot v}v=\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}v=-1\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x & =\\frac{x\\cdot w}{w\\cdot w}w=\\frac{(-3)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}}w=\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{v}\\,x+{\\text{proj}}_{w}\\,x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\frac{1}{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9a954e68-cdd4-5512-849a-e55e14c3f96e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518226}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518303 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186351463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28faabea-dfd0-55c2-85b3-adad07d107a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186348800} {:answer/id #uuid "55e962b4-4213-584d-8bfc-bfbc26a4d99e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349233} {:answer/id #uuid "700d4add-8f9b-56f7-9ad3-952853092eca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349476} {:answer/id #uuid "7a977362-a0b9-5918-829f-9fcce5294908" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186349574} {:answer/id #uuid "d9b37dbd-c83f-534f-9dde-b0d19a5de4ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186350356}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348800} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbf28350-f1e7-50ad-82d9-dcc4233c0637" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351148}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "bb8dc59e-a778-5f61-ad00-84a88b09a301" :question/math-academy-id "q-82912" :question/problem "Consider the vector $x$ and the subspace $S=\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,\\,x=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nFind the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ given that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal." :question/worked-solution "Since the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we first find the orthogonal projections of $x$ onto $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1}}$ and $\\text{Span}{{a}_{2}}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{1}}{{a}_{1}\\cdot {a}_{1}}{a}_{1}=\\frac{2\\cdot 0+3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 2}{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{(-1)}^{2}+{2}^{2}}{a}_{1}=2\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x & =\\frac{x\\cdot {a}_{2}}{{a}_{2}\\cdot {a}_{2}}{a}_{2}=\\frac{2\\cdot 3+3\\cdot 1+(-5)\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot (-1)}{{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & ={\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{1}}x+{\\text{proj}}_{{a}_{2}}x \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\hat{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance between $x$ and the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d(x,\\hat{x}) & =‖x-\\hat{x}‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{\\hat{x}}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{\\hat{x}}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{\\hat{x}}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{\\hat{x}}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-3)^{2}+(3-3)^{2}+(-5-(-3))^{2}+(2-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "da850a2d-b4a4-514e-8e22-54970af07ef4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518239}}] :activity/title "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Euclidean Spaces (Orthogonal Bases)" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517491}]}
